        "status": "Contact Oleg Drokin (green@whamcloud.com) with any questions on this account"
      },
      "date": "2026-10-13 13:19:02.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\n(1 comment)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good; one optional commit-message note inline, no need to re-spin for it.\n\n(suggestion) test_160f has the same pre-existing race this patch fixes in 160g/160h: it calls changelog_register twice back to back and then requires `[ $user_rec1 == $user_rec2 ]`, so a record arriving between the registrations fails it with the same \"index expected N, but is N+1\" error. Since this patch already fixes the pattern twice, would it make sense to apply the same treatment to 160f here or in a follow-up?",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 2
    },
