        "subject": "LU-20813 tests: fix changelog GC races in sanity 160g/160h",
        "message": "LU-20813 tests: fix changelog GC races in sanity 160g/160h\n\ntest_160g and test_160h register two changelog users back\nto back and required both to start at the same record\nindex, which fails whenever another record reaches the MDT\nin between. In test_160g that record also counts against\nthe first user's idle index limit, so clear the first user\nup to the second one's index instead of failing.\n\ntest_160h enabled GC with a 10 second idle limit before its\nremote setup commands, so slow nodes let GC deregister both\nusers before they were checked, or run an unblocked GC\nthread before fail_loc 0x1316 was set.\n\nAge only the second user with fault injection, which needs\nan MDS of 2.14.55 or later, and enable GC once the blocking\nfault is set and min_gc_interval has passed since the last\nGC check of the previous test. Drop the index check, write\none record to each MDT directly, since the filename hash\nmisses some stripes with many MDTs, wait for GC threads and\numounts to appear, and restart stopped MDTs on failure.\n\nFixes: 31fef6845e8b (\"LU-10680 mdd: create gc thread when no current transaction\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=\"160g 160h\",ONLY_REPEAT=10\nTest-Parameters: fstype=zfs mdtcount=4 mdscount=2 testlist=sanity\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I38cc2978b0ddbb7c1daecc8cbac75676eb9ce5ca\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
